d('b01',True,'The opening word plutôt has the appropriate tall stems and accent, while the dash is a single written horizontal. The final low body of topos is compressed against the closer; the blind topo cannot be excluded, so qualify the final s. In the cancelled neighbourhood sign, the round bowl and upper cap support the existing unsure script V; the crossing diagonal belongs to the cancellation and does not establish a separately recoverable X. The second-line closing curve and following comma remain, without an added exclamation.')
