d('b05',False,'The first bound relation has a separate lower bar; the final one is a heavily retraced less-than with no detached lower bar. The last k has two clear branches and a long hooked lower return. The return does not independently establish a cancelled j layer, so no old j is invented. All ell indices are closed loops, and the definition accent and formula number11 are retained.')
d('b06',True,'The full note has an opening parenthesis, one NB underline, the long-stemmed phi form and no stop after j=k. After k, the compressed short word and point favor succ.; additional reduced s/e-like curves also permit the independent success. reading, so retain that as an explicit abbreviation alternative. There is no full esseur ending or est un. The final closing curve remains separate.')
d('b07',False,'The large opening curve before On is distinct from its capital O. Ps- is raised and has a p, small s and hyphen, with no separate r/e body or accent to support pré-. Its leader attaches before partition. The inline def/déf label is crossed, but the two equality strokes remain in place before the opening brace. All looped ell forms, the existing < versus <= doubt and the final comma remain.')
d('b08',True,'The first label has a multi-arm star and one prime, while the second has two separate upper prime ticks despite retracing of its (k). Preserve those literal labels. The lower stroke of the first crossed containment sign is darkly doubled; the preferred not-superset remains, but a fused additional equality stroke cannot be excluded, so admit not-superseteq explicitly. The second containment sign has no crossing and remains unchanged.')
d('b09',True,'The first R index is a live descending j, not the revised i of formula10. The lower union prime count remains doubtful. The large oblique comma follows the lower summand and is not supplied after the brace. In the lower aussi formula, the R second index is unusually low and hump-shaped: k remains preferred by the same-page contracted k forms, but n is physically possible and is now explicit. Preserve the literal dotted X_i, not the expected X_j, and no final stop.')
d('b10',False,'The crossed sign still permits the rounded script V and ij, but no independent old X or subscript comma can be securely recovered. Formula13 has the same visible equalities, indices, stars and commas. D-où is above the line with a long leader into the third chain; this does not establish that every baseline symbol of that chain is an insertion. The final =Xi star wraps to the lower right with an open bent outline and small upper crossing stroke, retained by the first overlay. Differences of drawing coordinates and wrappers do not change the reading.')
d('b11',True,'The cancelled un remains tentative. All three singular homéomorphe/homotope endings have no independent s. The final de after affaibli has a long e exit, without a separate s. After germes and its comma is a distinct small dark loop with a short top stroke, before the separately begun qu-il; an enlarged view of this part of the existing blind crop confirms the independent o-like proposal. Add unsure o without assigning a meaning or a cancellation state. On voit has a low v/o, detached raised i and final t, not sait or est. Pouvant, the continuous g-descender of singulière, its period, the unmatched closing parenthesis and final formula comma remain.')
